    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379-a1">

                <pb facs="0642" n="1602" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 109.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr.
                            Pringle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I gathered from Mr. Straus, before his
                    departure, that Mr. Gillman, consul in Jerusalem, desired nothing further done
                    in reference to the eviction of his cavass from his house.</p>
                <p>I should like to know whether this is the case; if not, what is the present
                    status of the affair?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
